WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back, Mike!
-Thank you so much. Thank you.

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:05.438 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-So happy you're here.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:09.042
Before we move on to the show --
-Yes.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's World Cup time.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we actually met 2002...
-Yeah.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At a bar in L.A.
at a World Cup game.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:18.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you have a rooting
interest?

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.854 size:84% position:42%
Because we were there
to see England in 2002.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.389 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, I have England
as a rooting interest.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay. That's good.
-My parents are from England.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.092 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm actually a citizen.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:29.229 size:75% position:38%
I'm too into soccer.
This is my problem.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
It sort of affects
every part of --

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.465 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Oh, like emotionally?

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you bet your sweet bippy,
it does.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a pretty tense
first England game.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.572
I mean, they pulled it out,
but it was maybe a little closer

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
than you would want it to be.
-Yeah,

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.209 line:92%
I'm trying to wean off of it.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get too -- like,
when Liverpool got knocked out

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the -- I'm a Liverpool fan,
as well. Anybody?

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.716 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll take a sympathy "Whoo!"
Thank you.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It was during my birthday.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.390 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I was so bummed out.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.825 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But, you know, we, like,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.928
rented a bus for the tour
and I was just getting

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
the score, and we were,
like, losing.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:08.201
And then, Ramos fouled Salah.
Salah plays for Liverpool.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:11.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hurt himself.
-Hurt 'em. He got hurt.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Sorry, dude.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:15.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
He got taken out Mafia style
by Ramos.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just got sadder
and sadder.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.514
We got back to the house,
and Liverpool had lost.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.918
And it was like, you know --
everyone was doing like --

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.919 size:75% position:38% line:92%
♪♪ Happy birthday ♪♪

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.121 line:92%
♪♪ Happy birthday, dear Mike ♪♪

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.289 line:92%
And I'm like, "That was cheap.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.857 line:92%
That was a cheap, cheap play."

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:32.192 line:92%
And then, they were like --

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:35.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ [ Flatly ]
Happy birthday to you ♪♪

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Kelly is like, "Can I talk
to you for a second?"

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
My wife, Kelly.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Turn it around!
Turn it around!

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's ten people here!"
You Know, so...

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:46.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, would you --
if Canada was in the World Cup

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
and played England...
-Yeah.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...would you root
for Canada over England

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.511 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in a World Cup match?

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.046 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Wow, this is fantastic.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what if Canada put a man
on the moon?

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:01.621 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You know -- you know...

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:05.158 size:88% position:44%
We have a space shuttle.
It's an ice fishing hut.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.025 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:09.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not true. We have fantastic
technology in Canada.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.966
-I noticed, you're wearing a pin
that I'm familiar with because

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne Michaels wears this pin.
-Yes.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the Order of Canada
pin.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is indeed, yes.
-That's quite an honor.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:20.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is Canada's highest
civilian honor.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how -- when did you --
when were you --

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-It is, actually.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.545 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.780 line:92%
-When were you awarded yours?

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Last year.
-Oh, wow.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah,
on my birthday last year.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's great.
So this birthday really sucked

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.253 size:78% position:39%
compared to that one.
-It really sucked.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very proud to be Canadian.
-Of course.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:39.392 line:92%
-Um, uh, more so recently, too.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:49.169
I would like to remind everybody
that we have

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
the longest undefended border
in the world

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have the longest peace
treaties in the world.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.807 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah. Those are two
good things to have.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're your number-one
trading partner.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-On September 14th,

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:03.049
Canadian special forces were
in the ground in Afghanistan.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did not get attacked
ourselves,

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.519 line:92%
but we love America so much

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
that over 40,000 Canadians
served in Afghanistan.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
So these are just little facts
I'd like to point out.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:17.797 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Good hometown facts.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:21.601
-Not the stuff of security
threat, I think you'll find.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.971
-Yeah, no.
-But anyways, there, I said it.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.272 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.340 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I want to ask about --

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
we obviously saw
that "Gong Show" clip.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And you are --

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
you play in heavy makeup.
And last year,

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
in season one of this show,
it was not --

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
you did this without telling
anybody it was Mike Myers

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was playing the host
of the show.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I love "The Gong Show."

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was three shows
that I loved growing up --

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.889
"Saturday Night Live",
"Hockey Night in Canada",

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
and "The Gong Show."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I thought
"The Gong Show"

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:47.360 size:75% position:38% line:92%
was super punk rock.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it was, you know,
kind of, get in and get out,

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.097 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and somebody gets hurt.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:57.937
It was just a real -- just
a de-evolution of show business.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.772 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's anti-careerism.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:03.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's people flying
their freak flag.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.444 line:92%
You know? And it's what I did

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:07.113
with my brothers in kitchens
at parties to try and make

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
girls laugh,
you know what I mean?

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you surprised at who does
and doesn't get gonged?

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.119 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I'm totally surprised.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
But just getting back to why
I wanted to be Tommy

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that Chuck Barris
was my hero.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.325 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I read all of his books.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:21.294 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he kept maintaining,

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:24.430
I don't know if it's a fiction
or not, that he was in the CIA.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just thought
in the spirit of that,

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:29.869
what if we just pretended that
I was this guy, Tommy Maitland,

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.471 line:92%
give an elaborate back story.

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:33.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just, you know, it was
the sort of guy

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:36.209
that if something -- if somebody
is terrible on the show,

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:38.611 size:84% position:42%
he'll go, "I thought
you were breathtaking."

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:42.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"You've taken away my breath,
and I will need it back."

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:45.184
You know, and so I -- it's fun.
It's fun.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:49.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like two weeks
of silliness.

